From 895e758f7cf8cde5f78f4d5fbfb768bb4a33cb48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:22:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] workspace_source PR-2: secret scan matches every new object's
 entire raw bytes (no commit parsing)

Review 5891362210 (t_01a1d4eeb2658c6d) found a message line shaped like a
`gpgsig `/`mergetag ` header hid the indented lines after it, because
_commit_text parsed commits to drop signature continuations. Drop the
parser: the credential matcher now gets the ENTIRE raw bytes of every new
object from `cat-file --batch` (commit incl. all headers, signatures and
message; tag; tree; blob). The commit's tree line is still read, only to
locate new paths for the denylist and labels.

Nits: UTF-32-LE/BE without a BOM is decoded as text (NUL pattern by
4-byte position); embedded mergetag content is scanned (the whole object
is).

Tests (13 RED on 30cb7e2220): signature-shaped message lines (3 headers),
secret in a gpgsig block, mergetag tag message, UTF-32-LE/BE, and the
property test now plants secrets in extra headers, signature blocks,
signature-shaped message lines and mergetags (16 seeds). A real armor
signature does not trip the scan.
